  "fixture_ids": [
    "SR-FIX-NDJSON-NATIVE-CODEC-v1",
    "SR-FIX-NDJSON-STREAM-RESUME-v1"
  ],
  "preconditions": [
    "Caller-supplied complete UTF-8 byte source or explicit ordered envelopes; native resources use their existing schemas. No project, loader, live basis or authorization is supplied to this pure transport layer.",
    "Incremental feeds contain caller-owned immutable bytes; explicit finish or producer exhaustion declares actual EOF. Resume receives the original complete snapshot, stored cursor bytes and a separately retained cursor hash. Durable host storage and staging remain caller responsibilities."
  ],
  "steps": [
    "Decode multiple mixed native envelopes, re-encode their exact semantic values, compare canonical LF records and retain original source bytes/hash separately.",
    "Reject missing/extra/wrong transport fields, wrong payload kinds, incomplete native records, invalid local consistency, operations, result hashes and plan self-hashes without repair.",
    "Assert detached complete observations and no permission grant; trap file/network/process/write/generation/plan-execution calls and verify the same passive API in isolated Core and PYZ.",
    "Exercise arbitrary byte blocks, physical blank-line counting, strict JSON/UTF-8, valid EOF with/without LF and rejection of incomplete final records. Pauses and empty blocks remain incomplete.",
    "Persist source and cursor as inert caller-owned data, resume within UTF-8/escapes/numbers/records and at blank-line boundaries, and compare exactly ordered outputs without duplicates/skips. Reject changed source bytes, changed cursors, forged prefix skips and inconsistent cursor geometry before completion.",
    "Process a large line and repeated records without total-count/byte cutoffs; retain original resource/host exception classes and reject reuse after failure. Verify passive resume and the same API in isolated Core/PYZ while preserving all W oracles.",
    "Re-run the unchanged W/R behavior corpus and affected native JSON/plan/schema regressions after separating LF framing from strict JSON and native envelope validation; preserve physical diagnostics, cursor bytes, EOF/failure state, output order and passive boundaries."
  ],
  "oracle": {
    "kind": "behavior",
    "requirement_contract": "NDJSON-Import und -Export MÜSSEN pro Zeile genau ein versioniertes SpecRoad-Artefakt oder Change-Plan-Objekt verarbeiten, leere Zeilen ignorieren und Kommentare ablehnen.",
    "scope": "14.g.W/R/C passive native NDJSON v1 codec: all 28 native artifact kinds and regular plans retain values, versions, self-hashes, order, duplicates and original-byte provenance. Incremental feeds recognize only LF or explicit EOF, retain split UTF-8/escape/number bytes, report physical lines and hull-relative pointers, and never infer completion from pauses. Source-bound inert cursors revalidate consumed prefixes without re-emission; changed input/checkpoint bindings are conflict Code 6, malformed records/cursors Code 3, and resource/security exceptions retain their classes. No aggregate count/byte cutoff, write permission, file publication or implicit execution. Durable Work/CLI integration and higher import/export/model/manifest/authorization gates remain outside this codec proof."
  },
